This was perhaps my most promising game ever, as a lawful Valk
(seriously, they have it probably the easiest of all roles in the
early game!). Hit into a +1 orcish helm on DL1, after my kitty ate its
wearer and dropped the bloodstained helm at my feet. Got some iron
boots on DL3, also +1, and a leather armor. Upgraded that to elven
mithril on DL 7, having skipped the Mines for now to do Sokoban first.
(Something I find I survive much longer if I do!) Hit XL 7 in the
first level of Sokoban, so, suddenly remembering that I was lawful,
backtracked up one level and dipped to get Excalibur, which would
prove to be my weapon of choice for most of the game. Unfortunately it
was about here that my item-luck would hit a dry spell. I found a /
oFire in Sokoban, but used it up burning E and nuking the zoo, which
turned out to hold an "oReflection. So, at least I was no longer so
worried about the Gnome with the Wand of Death.

I continued down, finding a bones pile from one of my rogues, who had
nothing but starting gear and a pair of dwarven short swords. I took
the daggers, which, by sheer luck were still uncursed, and the sack. A
few levels deeper I hit into another bones pile, yielding a cursed -1
pair of speed boots and some wands which turned out to be fire, cold
and digging. On the same level I found a Hawaiian shirt and a katana,
which by dumb luck turned out to be blessed, and started using that in
my off hand. Somewhere in here I finally found a bag of holding, too.

I found the quest portal, but being still only XL 13, I continued
downward. Shortly thereafter I found Fort Ludios and cleaned out most
of it, but then I realized I had no way to cross the moat! My /oCold
was expended, I had no scrolls of charging or easy ways to get them, I
had no levitation or scrolls of earth, and no water walking, jumping
or magical breathing either. With some annoyance I backtracked,
leaving the 2 gray D behind, and continued down looking for some way
to cross the water, when I hit into an opulent throne room. Since I
had acquired perma-invisibility some time earlier, I snuck in and
murderized the occupants, one by one leaving the gray D for last. I
killed him and he left scales, so, combined with a ?oEA dropped by one
of the bugbears, I upgraded to GDSM. There was a =oLev here too,
whcih, although cursed, achieved my mission, and a +oID that was to be
very useful later. I found an unIDed wand in the loot pile too, and by
now the only wands I hadn't IDed were nothing, death and wishing.
Hoping for one of the last, but expecting the first, I engrave-tested
it. W00t, it was wishing! I promptly wished up 3 blessed charging
scrolls. I used the next two wishes (luckily it came 0:3) on a blessed
fixed +3 pair of dex gaunts, since I still had no gloves (making
cockatrices an even dicier affair, since it was a new moon!), and the
blessed fixed +2 Magicbane for engraving E and a backup source of MR.
This did, however, pretty much burn up my shot at artiwishing, since
now my game had Excalibur, Mojo and Magicbane, and would soon have the
Orb of Fate. I recharged it, and knowing I still had the castle wand
ahead, and wished up a trio of geno scrolls, a robe to replace my now-
useless invis cloak (since I had invis intrinsically) and a magic
marker, saving the wrest charge for anything I might have forgotten.

This in hand, I went back to Ludios and cleaned out its throne room
and vault, netting tons of gold, a /oCold and another marker. So, I
did the quest (Surtur is a weenie!), then went back up to a co-aligned
altar on DL12 to bless and enchant some stuff, and sac more hoping for
Grayswandir. (I never did get another sac gift, despite some hundred
sacrifices!). I also bought 9 points of protection and prayed up
another one. Confident in my abilities I headed back down, wasted
Medusa summarily while blinded with a towel. Unlike a samurai I lost
earlier, I made sure she was dead before de-toweling despite the fact
that I had reflection. On downward I went, blessed-genoing Liches
first, then hit the castle, and blessed-genoed ; just to be sure.
Rather than frak around with the dangerous drawbridge I just blew it
away with force bolt from long range then proceeded to levitate over
the moat and hack away, using force bolt on anything that I thought
would be dangerous. One of the soldiers bounced a /oFire off me
halfway through and cooked a bunch of his own allies, then I waded in
and finished off the monsters. The dragons were red, white and black,
who all left scales. (Yeah, now that I don't need 'em!). Got the wand,
wished up a BGF +3 helm of brilliance, and got it. Alas, this was the
only charge in the wand, so I re-oomphed it, wished up two more
markers, blew the wrest charge of my last wand on another one, then
saved the remaining charge+wrest in the castle wand for a rainy day.

I went back up, enchanted myself stupid, had a near-disaster with a ?
oEW that left me with the +8 Excalibur (instead of a handful of sword
vapor, luckily!). Armed with a +8 Excalibur and a +7 katana, I went
back down, cleared out the VoTD and headed into Gehennom, which was
pretty uneventful. I wasted Vlad, though since this was my first time
getting to him, I didn't play around and just handed him his head on a
shield of reflection :) Since I now had a zillion more scrolls to
blank, I levelported back up to enchant my armor some more. However,
it was at this point that I made a fatal mistake. I had taken off all
my armor except my shirt to enchant that more. I also switched my
"oReflection for a "oLS, wanting some typo resistance. As I stood
there, in an empty room (mistake 1) enchanting, a gnome popped in and
zotted me with a /oDeath. I lifesaved, then panicked. Now, at this
point, I had a large number of things I could have done to save
myself. I could have wielded Magicbane. I could have put my
"oReflection on. I could have zapped the gnome with /my/ wand of
death, or just teleported him away, or teleported myself. I could have
tossed daggers, or zapped a wand of cold, or even taken one step
toward him to melee. But no. I, in my infinite stupidity, decided
'ZOMG, gotta get my GDSM back on, stat'. Now, as anyone with an ounce
of sense knows, this takes some time, and you don't get MR until it's
fully on. Well, one turn later, DYWYPI?

Cue much dancing and cursing and swearing. This was my closest one
yet, and I almost certainly would have ascended had this little piss-
ant gnome not gotten in my way! By the time I croaked, I would have
had -44 AC fully armored, and about 280HP from some nurse-dancing in
Sokoban and a bit of alchemizing. I also had a +3 silver saber that
I'd found in Gehennom, which might have made things easier. No
Grayswandir, but then, there's no shame in ascending with Excalibur :)



